+# CutFlow v12.4 — Customer privacy / automatic de-identification
+
+## What changes
+
+- Walk-ins no longer create a permanent record in the `customers` table.
+- A walk-in's name, phone and notes exist only while the queue item is active. Pressing **Complete** replaces the name with `Serviced customer` and clears the phone and notes.
+- Appointment customers remain identifiable only while CutFlow still needs their details for an active appointment or queue item.
+- Pressing **Completed** on an appointment removes the customer link and appointment notes, deletes appointment notifications, and anonymizes the customer profile when there are no other active bookings/queue entries for that customer.
+- Anonymous operational data such as service, staff, date/time, price, payment status and queue timing remains available for business reporting.
+- Existing completed appointments and walk-ins are cleaned by the upgrade SQL.
+
+## Important product effect
+
+CutFlow can no longer reliably use completed customer identity for repeat-customer CRM, loyalty continuity or post-service marketing. This is intentional: the new privacy rule prioritizes removal of identifiable customer data after service.
+
+## Apply to an existing Supabase project
+
+Run the complete file below in Supabase SQL Editor:
+
+`supabase/UPGRADE_V12_4_CUSTOMER_PRIVACY.sql`
+
+Then deploy the updated application source. The dashboard's **Complete** actions call the new privacy-safe database functions, so the SQL upgrade and app deployment should be applied together.
